<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92150" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥαμνοῦς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦντος</span> (
			contr.
		 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥαμνόεις</span>), ὁ, <u>Rhamnus</u>, a deme in Attica
		(named from the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥάμνοι</span> growing in it),
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐν Ῥ. θεός</span>, i.e. Nemesis,
			<i><span class="en">
			Paus.
			1.33.2
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			9.1.17
		</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
			22
		</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥαμνοῦντι</span>, not <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Ῥ.</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at Rhamnus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				19.28
			</span></i>, etc.—Hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥαμνούσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <u>Rhamnusian</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.157
			</span></i>, etc.; ἡ</div>
